    {
      "id": "note-1",
      "courseId": "course-cs101",
      "title": "Mastering Big-O Analysis & Master Theorem Cheat Sheet",
      "content": "### Master Theorem Quick Reference\nFor recurrences of the form $T(n) = aT(n/b) + f(n)$ where $a \\ge 1$ and $b > 1$:\n1. **Case 1**: If $f(n) = O(n^{\\log_b a - \\epsilon})$ for $\\epsilon > 0$, then $T(n) = \\Theta(n^{\\log_b a})$.\n2. **Case 2**: If $f(n) = \\Theta(n^{\\log_b a} \\log^k n)$ with $k \\ge 0$, then $T(n) = \\Theta(n^{\\log_b a} \\log^{k+1} n)$.\n3. **Case 3**: If $f(n) = \\Omega(n^{\\log_b a + \\epsilon})$ and regularity condition holds ($af(n/b) \\le c f(n)$ for $c < 1$), then $T(n) = \\Theta(f(n))$.\n\n*Exam Tip:* Always check if $b$ is a divisor or a subtraction. If $T(n) = T(n-1) + O(1)$, this is linear $O(n)$, not logarithmic!",
      "tags": [
        "Algorithms",
        "Complexity",
        "Exam Prep"
      ],
      "confirmCount": 3,
      "flagCount": 0,
      "confidenceScore": 3,
      "createdAt": "2026-08-17T04:14:02.239Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "note-2",
      "courseId": "course-cs201",
      "title": "Red-Black Tree Invariants & Rotation Mechanics",
      "content": "### 5 Properties of Red-Black Trees:\n1. Every node is either red or black.\n2. The root is always black.\n3. Every leaf (NIL node) is black.\n4. If a node is red, both its children are black (no two consecutive reds).\n5. Every path from a given node to any of its descendant NIL nodes contains the same number of black nodes (Black-Height).\n\n**Max Height Proof:** Height is at most $2 \\log_2(n + 1)$, guaranteeing $O(\\log n)$ search, insert, and delete operations.",
      "tags": [
        "Data Structures",
        "Trees",
        "C++"
      ],
      "confirmCount": 1,
      "flagCount": 0,
      "confidenceScore": 1,
      "createdAt": "2026-08-19T04:14:02.239Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "note-3",
      "courseId": "course-math220",
      "title": "Eigenvalues, Eigenvectors & Diagonalization Steps",
      "content": "### Diagonalization Workflow:\n1. Find characteristic polynomial: $\\det(A - \\lambda I) = 0$.\n2. Solve for eigenvalues $\\lambda_1, \\lambda_2, \\dots, \\lambda_k$.\n3. For each $\\lambda_i$, find basis of nullspace: $(A - \\lambda_i I)\\vec{v} = \\vec{0}$.\n4. If geometric multiplicity equals algebraic multiplicity for all eigenvalues, matrix $A$ is diagonalizable: $A = PDP^{-1}$ where $P$ has eigenvectors as columns and $D$ has eigenvalues along diagonal.",
      "tags": [
        "Linear Algebra",
        "Matrices",
        "Formulas"
      ],
      "confirmCount": 18,
      "flagCount": 2,
      "confidenceScore": 16,
      "createdAt": "2026-08-18T04:14:02.239Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "note-4",
      "courseId": "course-bio110",
      "title": "Krebs Cycle & ATP Yield Breakdown (Aerobic Respiration)",
      "content": "### Total Net ATP Yield per Glucose Molecule:\n- **Glycolysis**: 2 ATP (net) + 2 NADH (~3-5 ATP via ETC)\n- **Pyruvate Oxidation**: 2 NADH (~5 ATP)\n- **Citric Acid (Krebs) Cycle**: 2 GTP (converted to 2 ATP) + 6 NADH (~15 ATP) + 2 FADH2 (~3 ATP)\n- **Total Theoretical Yield**: ~30 to 32 ATP per glucose molecule.\n\n*Common Mistake:* Remember that each NADH yields ~2.5 ATP while each FADH2 yields only ~1.5 ATP because FADH2 enters at Complex II instead of Complex I.",
      "tags": [
        "Cellular Bio",
        "Metabolism",
        "Cheat Sheet"
      ],
      "confirmCount": 12,
      "flagCount": 1,
      "confidenceScore": 11,
      "createdAt": "2026-08-20T04:14:02.239Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "note-5",
      "courseId": "course-econ101",
      "title": "Price Elasticity of Demand & Total Revenue Relationship",
      "content": "### Elasticity Formula:\n$$\\epsilon_d = \\frac{\\% \\Delta Q}{\\% \\Delta P} = \\frac{(Q_2 - Q_1) / [(Q_2 + Q_1) / 2]}{(P_2 - P_1) / [(P_2 + P_1) / 2]}$$\n\n### Revenue Effect:\n- If $|\\epsilon_d| > 1$ (Elastic): Price $\\uparrow \\implies$ Revenue $\\downarrow$.\n- If $|\\epsilon_d| = 1$ (Unitary): Price change has zero net effect on revenue (revenue is maximized).\n- If $|\\epsilon_d| < 1$ (Inelastic): Price $\\uparrow \\implies$ Revenue $\\uparrow$.",
      "tags": [
        "Microeconomics",
        "Elasticity",
        "Formulas"
      ],
      "confirmCount": 7,
      "flagCount": 0,
      "confidenceScore": 7,
      "createdAt": "2026-08-21T04:14:02.239Z"
    }
